Variant 1: restrict PR #144587's PAUSE swap to Linux/x86 only.
Branch: yield-linux-only (1 commit on main). Verdict: still regresses contended
FT locks (see FINDINGS.md §2); scoping fix only, not a real fix.

diff --git a/Include/internal/pycore_lock.h b/Include/internal/pycore_lock.h
index 7dd2419ecec..03aad1d8cd1 100644
--- a/Include/internal/pycore_lock.h
+++ b/Include/internal/pycore_lock.h
@@ -75,8 +75,21 @@ PyMutex_LockFlags(PyMutex *m, _PyLockFlags flags)
 // error messages) otherwise returns 0.
 extern int _PyMutex_TryUnlock(PyMutex *m);

-// Yield the processor to other threads (e.g., sched_yield).
+// Yield the processor while spinning in a lock's spin-wait loop.
+//
+// On Linux/x86, sched_yield() is a real syscall (~hundreds of ns), so we
+// instead emit the lightweight PAUSE spin-wait hint (measured ~3-19ns, vs
+// ~250-650ns for sched_yield()). Every other platform keeps the out-of-line
+// OS scheduler yield (SwitchToThread / sched_yield) defined in Python/lock.c:
+// on Darwin sched_yield() is a cheap fast-trap that measured faster than a
+// bare pause and additionally hands the core to the lock holder, and no other
+// arch's pause hint has been benchmarked in this loop yet.
+#if defined(__linux__) && (defined(__x86_64__) || defined(__i386__))
+#  define _Py_YIELD_INLINE 1
+static inline void _Py_yield(void) { __asm__ volatile ("pause" ::: "memory"); }
+#else
 extern void _Py_yield(void);
+#endif


 // PyEvent is a one-time event notification
diff --git a/Misc/NEWS.d/next/Core_and_Builtins/2026-08-15-10-05-00.gh-issue-144586.Lnx86Y.rst b/Misc/NEWS.d/next/Core_and_Builtins/2026-08-15-10-05-00.gh-issue-144586.Lnx86Y.rst
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..0ed114c978d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Misc/NEWS.d/next/Core_and_Builtins/2026-08-15-10-05-00.gh-issue-144586.Lnx86Y.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@
+On Linux/x86, ``_Py_yield()`` now emits the lightweight ``PAUSE`` spin-wait
+hint inside a lock's spin-wait loop instead of calling the
+:manpage:`sched_yield(2)` syscall. Other platforms keep the OS scheduler
+yield. Patch by Donghee Na.
